Subject: [PATCH] Sharding

Split one world across several Reef servers behind a Velocity proxy.
The logic lives in dev.reef.sharding.Sharding; this patch adds the hooks:

- ServerPlayer#doTick: check every tick whether the player crossed into
  another shard's region, and hand them over.
- PlayerList#remove: clean up handoff state.
- ServerLevel#mayInteract: players can't change blocks in other shards'
  regions or within the border protection strip.
- ServerLevel entity ticking: mobs in other shards' regions are frozen.
- ServerLevel#tickChunk / ServerChunkCache#tickSpawningChunk: no random
  ticks or natural spawning in chunks another shard simulates.
- PlayerDataStorage: optional player data folder shared by all shards;
  don't save players again after they've been handed off.

Configured in the sharding section of reef.yml. Off by default.

